You can run code when your FastAPI application starts up or shuts down using the `lifespan` parameter of the `FastAPI` app, and a "context manager" [4]. 

Alternatively, you can declare event handler functions with the `on_event` decorator, like this:

```python
@app.on_event("startup")
def startup_event():
    # Code to run when the application starts up

@app.on_event("shutdown")
def shutdown_event():
    # Code to run when the application shuts down
```

Note that the `startup` and `shutdown` event handlers will no longer be called if you provide a `lifespan` parameter to the `FastAPI` app [2].
